Almost perfect. Three "regressions" — all in `js/unit-tests/test_dfManager.js`, caused by my additions to `makeDfManager` (the `opts.files` branch in fileReadMock and `opts.cliThrow` in cli_execute_command). These are TEST-file functions; they're in the CRAP baseline too (the ratchet covers everything including tests). `makeDfManager` 9.3 → 12 would FAIL the CI ratchet (CRAP grew vs baseline).

Fix: reduce the complexity I added to makeDfManager/fileReadMock/cli_execute_command — extract branches. The cleanest approach: move the extended logic OUT of the closures into module-level helper functions in the test file:

```js
// module-level
function dfFileReadMock(opts, files, smConfigRaw) { ... }
``

But closures capture `written`, etc. The mock functions only need `opts` — let me extract:

```js
// gh-1198: module-level mock bodies keep makeDfManager's CRAP at its
// baseline (the ratchet covers test files too).
function dfReadFile(opts, readOpts) {
   var path = typeof readOpts === 'string' ? readOpts : readOpts.path;
   if (opts.files && opts.files[path] !== undefined) return opts.files[path];
   if (path === 'agents/sm.json') {
       return JSON.stringify({...});
   }
   return null;
}
``

And in makeDfManager: `file_read: function(readOpts) { return dfReadFile(opts, readOpts); }` — CC of the closure = 1.

cli_execute_command:
```js
function dfExecCommand(opts, commands, args) {
   commands.push(args.command);
   if (opts.cliThrow) throw new Error(opts.cliThrow);
   return '';
}
``
Closure CC = 1.

Then makeDfManager returns to CC ~ previous (9.3 baseline). fileReadMock closure CC 1 (baseline was 3.1 — fine, can only improve), cli_execute_command closure CC 1 (was 1.3).

Wait — but the ratchet for functions that SHRINK is fine (never grows). makeDfManager itself: I didn't add branches to it (only nested closure bodies) — makeDfManager's own CC grew 9.3→12 because the closures count towards it. Moving bodies to module level restores it.

Actually let me check the AFTER report entries for test_dfManager to see exact current values.

